  "entry": "code/calcFSC.py",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Computes the Fourier Shell Correlation curve between two uploaded half maps and draws confidence bounds from one of three statistical methods (Fisher z, bootstrap, analytical variance), so the 0.143 resolution can be read with its uncertainty and exported as CSV. Sigma sets the bound width for Fisher z and analytical variance; bootstrap always gives a 95% percentile interval. Data used in the run: none. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
